## Where to find it

Everything below sits in the **Timetable** group in the side drawer. Which items you see there
depends on your access level — the grid, class subjects, curriculum and configuration are each
separately permissioned, so an admin may see all four while a coordinator sees only one or two.

Teachers don't normally use this section at all. They get **My Timetable** as its own top-level
drawer item instead — a read-only view of their own week.

## The order to do things in

The timetable grid can only place lessons that the surrounding configuration already knows about,
so a new institute usually works outwards from the setup screens:

1. **Configuration → Bell Schedule** — define the periods that make up a day (label, start and end
   time, and whether the period is a break). You can keep more than one schedule and mark one as
   the default.
2. **Grade Curriculum** — what each grade is meant to be taught.
3. **Class Subjects** — which subjects actually run for each individual class.
4. **Timetable Grid** — place those subjects into periods.

If a subject isn't offered when you try to place it, the fix is almost always in Class Subjects or
Grade Curriculum rather than in the grid itself.

## Working in the grid

- Each cell is one class in one period on one day. Selecting a cell lets you set the lesson there,
  or place a whole **subject group** when several classes split into options at the same time.
- **Copy day** takes every slot on one day and repeats it on the days you choose. The confirmation
  tells you how many slots copied and how many were **skipped as conflicts** — skipped slots are
  ones where the target period was already occupied or the teacher was already booked, so nothing
  is silently overwritten.
- When a change would double-book a teacher or a classroom, the grid refuses it and highlights the
  clashing slot rather than saving both.

## Other configuration tabs

**Configuration** carries more than the bell schedule:

- **Teacher Constraints** — when individual teachers are and aren't available.
- **Subjects & Rules** and **Subject Groups** — how subjects behave and which ones are offered as a
  set of options.
- **Classrooms** — the rooms lessons can be matched to.
- **Import Data** — bulk-load setup data instead of entering it screen by screen.

You can also export the finished timetable for **all classes** or for **all teachers** from the top
of the Configuration screen.

